# API Design

## Conventions

- RESTful resources: `/api/v1/vehicles`, `/api/v1/rentals`, `/api/v1/rentals/:id/handovers`.
- Use HTTP verbs correctly: GET (read), POST (create/action), PATCH (partial update), DELETE (remove).
- Nouns for resources; verbs only for non-CRUD actions (`POST /rentals/:id/approve-pickup`).

## Request/response

- Every request body validated via DTO class.
- Consistent success envelope: `{ data: T }` or paginated `{ data: T[], meta: { page, total } }`.
- Consistent error envelope: `{ statusCode, message, errorCode?, details? }`.
- Use appropriate HTTP status codes (400 validation, 401 unauth, 403 forbidden, 404 not found, 409 conflict for duplicate CNIC/rating).

## Authorization per endpoint

| Endpoint type | Check |
|---------------|-------|
| Public discovery | No CNIC, no exact owner address |
| Own profile | User can read/update own data including CNIC |
| Rental agreement | Only owner + renter participants; includes mutual CNIC |
| Handover photos | Only rental participants; owner uploads, renter approves |
| Ratings | Only after rental completed; one per side |

## Pagination & filtering

- Cursor or offset pagination for vehicle discovery and rental lists.
- Filter/query params validated as DTOs; never pass raw client strings to Prisma.

## Idempotency

- State transition endpoints should be safe to retry (check current state before transitioning).
- Use 409 Conflict when an action is invalid for the current state.
